// GPU settings preset: medium
//
// A texture edge of 2048 voxels and 8 GB of texture memory. 2048 is the
// largest edge that the presets assume a device can render, so `medium` and
// `high` differ only by memory. A device of the middle class crashed with
// more texture memory than 8 GB.
//
// A preset applies only with final downsampling on, and a preset in this
// customization turns final downsampling on, also in a locked-down config.
// `?customization=` needs `customizationUrlPrefixes`, and config/default.js has
// none: there, set the preset through `customizationService` in the config.
// Nothing probes the device: a preset is a set of values, so a real device may
// hold more or less than the preset states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/medium`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuSettingsPreset": "medium"
  }
}
